REQUIRES: msbuild
XFAIL: *

Without a generator, CMake on Windows picks the newest installed Visual
Studio, so the build runs through MSBuild and its CL task. CMAKE_GENERATOR
is cleared so the developer environment cannot override that choice.
Known failures: #123 (MSBuild compiles through response files).

RUN: %e2e prepare hello %t
RUN: env -u CMAKE_GENERATOR cmake -S %t -B %t/build
RUN: %catter script::cdb -v -o %t/compile_commands.json -- cmake --build %t/build --config Debug
RUN: %e2e summarize %t/compile_commands.json %t | FileCheck %s

CHECK: entries: 2
CHECK-NEXT: other entries: 0
CHECK-NEXT: src/main.cc exists dir={{.+}} output={{.+}} define=yes
CHECK-NEXT: src/util.cc exists dir={{.+}} output={{.+}} define=yes
